"""Heavy fire support part 1: the air attacks and artillery strikes (game/heavy_fire_support.cpp) against the original's
(script/hf_diff.cpp, suite heavy.fire). Run: on script/build_hf.bat, the full 1,500 cases; MUT_HARNESS script,
MUT_EXTRA_SRCS original_exe.cpp and hf_calls.s, MUT_LDFLAGS -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000; MUT_PASS
"hf_diff: .*, N checks, 0 failures".

557 mutants, 67 not building; 445 of the 490 building killed at first, 453 after the test was widened (odd frame
times: the timers land on 1 and one past their ends; the radio's file names logged as text). The 37 left:
- The port's fixes: values before a kind's model and kinds past 16 (469 and, 475 cmp: the original writes outside
  the table; not given); the flags past the four (514 and: the original writes the byte after the object); a kind past
  the table in a message (646 cmp: the original reads past it).
- Equivalent: the defaults set again (150..155 del, 457 del: the module is made once, its kinds default already);
  members already so (96, 112, 219, 234 del); an effect for a fourth case of rand() % 3 (78 num); (void)caller (133
  del); the global module's name (139 text: the test makes its own module; the original's global is never made);
  the lead plane's w and the requests' target w, never read (182 del, 526 num); deletions no one sees (162, 255, 583,
  624 del, 623 num: the destructors do nothing visible); the radio's tests (283, 392 and: the speech and its timer
  exist only with a caller on a client); LoadTable's answer and its first ids (452, 455, 464, 468, 508 bool, 453, 466
  num: no one reads them; a failing Descend returns first); the name buffer's size (472 num); the chunk's destructor
  closes it (506, 507 del)."""
